-12","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Edwin F. Negron-Carballo","x":"The note receivable is part of an agreement executed with our China distributor related to the restructuring of our business relationship to a royalty based model, which requires the repayment over five year period of the investment the company made in China during the 2017 and 2018 years.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/11/12/celsius-holdings-inc-celh-q3-2020-earnings-call-tr/"},{"c":"CELH 2021 Q2","e":"celh","d":"2021-08-12","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"John Fieldly","x":"When we look at pricing right now, we're really watching what the other players in the category are doing and also same with Monster and many players really watching our promotional allocations, allowances and plans as we go forward to mitigate the overall frontline price increase.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/12/celsius-holdings-inc-celh-q2-2021-earnings-call-tr/"},{"c":"CELH 2021 Q2","e":"celh","d":"2021-08-12","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Sean King","x":"I'll pass it on.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/12/celsius-holdings-inc-celh-q2-2021-earnings-call-tr/"},{"c":"CELH 2021 Q2","e":"celh","d":"2021-08-12","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Edwin F. Negron-Carballo","x":"Other international markets generated $62,000 in revenue during the three months ended June 30, 2021, a decrease of $45,000 from $107,000 for the prior year quarter, mainly related to an operational restructuring in the Middle East.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/08/12/celsius-holdings-inc-celh-q2-2021-earnings-call-tr/"},{"c":"CELH 2021 Q3","e":"celh","d":"2021-11-11","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"John Fieldly","x":"The smaller scale new entrants pay significant higher shipping, raw materials, co-pack fees, competition and by not taking price, the top two energy drinks place an outsized cost on the new entrants entering the market to protect their share.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/11/celsius-holdings-inc-celh-q3-2021-earnings-call-tr/"},{"c":"CELH 2021 Q3","e":"celh","d":"2021-11-11","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"John Fieldly","x":"Additional incremental near-term benefits will be recognized if price increases are initiated by the top brands to our 2022 expectation.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/11/celsius-holdings-inc-celh-q3-2021-earnings-call-tr/"},{"c":"CELH 2025 Q3","e":"celh","d":"2025-11-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Jarrod Langhans","x":"…the lapping benefits of the prior year inventory optimization, lower net portfolio promotional spend, pack mix, favorable channel mix and scale benefits on raw materials from higher volume, partially offset by tariffs and the impact of Alani Nu and Rockstar Energy's lower margin profiles.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/11/27/celsius-celh-q3-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CELH 2025 Q3","e":"celh","d":"2025-11-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Jarrod Langhans","x":"We anticipate Q4 will be a noisy quarter, reflecting year-end timing effects from promotions, integration activities and cash management from our larger customers, along with some incremental freight and tariff pressure.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2025/11/27/celsius-celh-q3-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CELH 2025 Q4","e":"celh","d":"2026-02-26","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Jarrod Langhans","x":"…47.4%, compared to 50.2% in the prior year period, reflecting dilution from Rockstar Energy, higher cost of product related to integration costs and tariffs, partially offset by improved outbound freight, lower consolidation billbacks as a percentage of revenue and favorable product impact mix.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/26/celsius-celh-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CELH 2025 Q4","e":"celh","d":"2026-02-26","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Jarrod Langhans","x":"…initiatives take hold, we expect margins to expand across 2026 and return to a more normalized profile, with gross margins in the low 50s driven by savings across raw materials, scrap, manufacturing tolling fees, freight and package and brand mix, offset in part by tariffs and aluminum costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/26/celsius-celh-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CELH 2025 Q4","e":"celh","d":"2026-02-26","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jarrod Langhans","x":"Revenue growth management for us is not about broad-based price increases.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/26/celsius-celh-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CELH 2026 Q3","e":"celh","d":"2026-11-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jarrod Langhans","x":"Price is a part of that infrastructure and a part of that program, but not necessarily the biggest driver and not necessarily where we are just saying we are taking price everywhere.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/05/celsius-celh-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"CELH 2026 Q3","e":"celh","d":"2026-11-05","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Jarrod Langhans","x":"It is all about going account by account and really working to see what is the best position we can put the portfolio in, whether it is about price pack architecture, different promotions, price increases, those kind of things.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/05/celsius-celh-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/"}],"trends":{"theater":[[36,1,8881,0,0,0,7271,982],[38,1,6926,0,0,0,6118,558],[39,1,9289,0,0,0,8233,747],[40,1,7815,0,0,0,6865,661],[41,1,7289,0,0,0,5654,1252],[42,1,8252,0,0,0,6860,1070],[43,1,8576,0,0,0,7312,961],[44,1,7714,0,0,0,6729,715],[45,1,7684,0,0,0,6443,912],[46,1,7552,0,0,0,6506,713],[47,1,